# deploy repo — .gitignore
#
# This repo is PUBLIC git (IRD-017 §Bootstrap: Argo CD needs no repo secret), so
# the cost of an accidental commit is higher here than anywhere else in the
# program. gitleaks is the real gate (secret-scan.yml, unfiltered); this file
# just keeps the obvious things out of a `git add .`.

# ---- Helm ----
# Dependency charts pulled by `helm dependency update` / kustomize's --enable-helm.
# Vendored chart tarballs are build output, not source; the pinned version in
# Chart.yaml / kustomization.yaml IS the source of truth.
charts/*/charts/
charts/**/*.tgz
# NOTE: Chart.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — commit it so dependency
# versions are reproducible across machines and CI (same rule as
# iac-platform's .terraform.lock.hcl).

# ---- Kustomize / render output ----
# `kustomize build ... > out.yaml` while debugging. The rendered manifests are
# derived state — Argo re-renders from source on every sync. Committing them
# would create a second source of truth that silently goes stale.
rendered/
*.rendered.yaml
out.yaml

# ---- Cluster credentials ----
# Nothing here should ever hold a kubeconfig, but the k3s one is fetched to a
# working dir during D12's bootstrap and a stray copy must never land in a
# PUBLIC repo.
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.kube/

# ---- Secrets ----
# ESO materializes real secrets INTO the cluster from SSM (IRD-019); this repo
# only ever holds ExternalSecret CRs, which contain references, not values.
# A file matching these patterns means something went wrong.
*.env
!*.env.example
secrets.yaml
*-secret.yaml
!*-externalsecret.yaml

# ---- OS / editor ----
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
